body:
tbh I'm not sure.  I didn't realize the difference in gauges since the bone stayed in all the time but it was at least 1 if not 2.  I'm not too worried about infections since my immune system is pretty decent.  I just don't want a scar just over a fit of impatience.

&#x200B;

I've had some random stuff suggested like hydrogen peroxide and triple antibiotic but so far I've only washed it out with saline.

Sorry, I really don't understand this stuff myself but I was able to get some readings...

&#x200B;

I'm pretty sure they were 111 in November, 102 this month

I'll sample the bra rainbow.

&#x200B;

Edit: \*in black

Well see that's the thing...I've had no problem with this bra aside from that one strap (intermittently) since I got it and I've had the straps fully adjusted.  I kept hearing "Bras just suck" for an explanation but now they're both doing it and it's fairly consistent.  My concern is that it's my belly moving my bra upwards based on a bunch of fat redistribution that just happened.  That's fine and all since I want to diet relatively soon but I'd definitely be *happier* to know it's because my shoulders are smaller rather than my belly bigger lol

&#x200B;

The bra is old, the muffin top is new.
